# Rust build output and deployed cartridge content, in any crate folder
# (e.g. launcher/target, launcher/output).
target/
output/

# WebView2's engine cache folder, wherever it lands in the tree.
EBWebView/

# Signing keys. `xtask keygen` puts the secret key outside the working tree
# entirely and refuses to write one inside it, so this is the second lock on a
# door that should already be shut — but a signing key reaching a public repo is
# unrecoverable (every listener built against it would have to be replaced), and
# one line here is cheap insurance.
*.key
.env

# The public half of a locally generated key. Harmless to publish, but it is
# *your* key: a listener built from this tree trusts it, and committing it would
# quietly ask everyone else's build to trust it too. keys/gacasy.pub — the
# release key — is tracked, and is the only one that should be.
keys/